title:: BMInOutArray
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - an ordered Dictionary of named inputs or outputs
categories:: Classes

Description::

BMInOutArray is an ordered Dictionary of named inputs or outputs and is used to represent the input or output busses of objects in the BEASTmulch Library. Members of the collection should be either instances of Association, in the form name->busIndex, or instances of the link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMSpeaker:: class, which mimics Association polymorphically.

In most cases members can be accessed by either key or index. For this reason numbers are not valid keys for use in this class. (Symbols are the expected key class in most places in the library in any case.)

BMInOutArray also provides support for named subarrays, specified as lists of keys.

In the current implementation no distinction is made between audio and control busses, and it is assumed that users will distinguish appropriately.

See also: link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMSpeaker::, link::Classes/Association::, link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMHardwareInputsProxy::, link::Classes/Bus::, link::Classes/List::, link::Classes/Dictionary::, link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMSpeakerListVisualiser::

Section:: Compatibility

BMInOutArray responds to strong::asUGenInput::,  strong::asControlInput::, strong::asOSCArgBundle::, and strong::asOSCArgArray:: by returning an link::Classes/Array:: of its member's bus indices. It can thus be used directly in most places where you would pass such an Array. For example:

code::
// make a BMInOutArray with two members
i = BMInOutArray.new;
i.add(BMSpeaker(\left, 0));
i.add(BMSpeaker(\right, 1));
// make a Synth
(
x = {|outs = #[3, 4]| 
	y = SinOsc.ar([440, 660], 0, 0.2);
	outs.do({|out, i| Out.ar(out, y[i])});
}.play;
)
x.set(\outs, i);
::
	
Section:: asBMInOutArray

Many classes in the BEASTMulch library which manage busses (e.g. audio sources, controllers) understand the message asBMInOutArray and return an array which corresponds to their outputs. The class link::Classes/Bus:: is extended to implement it as well as a convenience method, and takes a single name argument as the base name for its keys:

code::
b = Bus.audio(s, 12);
a = b.asBMInOutArray(\myPrivateBusaho);
::

Similarly, Server is extended to include two methods: strong::insAsBMInOutArray::, and strong::outsAsBMInOutArray::. The former returns a link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMHardwareInputsProxy::, and the latter a BMInOutArray corresponding to the server's hardware output busses.

code::
s.insAsBMInOutArray;
s.outsAsBMInOutArray;
::

Section:: Implementation Notes

BMInOutArray is a subclass of link::Classes/List::, rather than a subclass of link::Classes/Dictionary:: although it understands most methods of the latter. Its key list is lazily constructed. This keeps the implementation simpler, and also means that BMSpeakers in the array can change their names (keys) without needing the array to be updated, but means that for very large collections it will be notably slower than say an link::Classes/IdentityDictionary::. Since input and output collections are likely to be relatively small (i.e. < 100 elements), this should not pose a particular problem in normal usage.

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: new
Create a new BMInOutArray. In many cases you can get these directly from other objects in the library.

argument:: size
An initial capacity for the object.

code::		
// make a new BMInOutArray
i = BMInOutArray.new;
i.add(\foo->1); // add an Association
i.add(BMSpeaker(\bar, 2)); // add a BMSpeaker
i[\foobar] = 3; // C-style syntax also works
i[\foo];
i[\bar];
i[2]; // can also lookup values by index
::

method:: hardwareInputArray
Returns an instance of link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMHardwareInputsProxy:: corresponding to the hardware inputs for the specified server. The values of the Association pairs will be the indices of the hardware input busses.

argument:: server
The link::Classes/Server:: whose hardware inputs will be represented.
argument:: name
A link::Classes/String:: or like::Classes/Symbol:: to use as the base name. Default value is "Hardware In".

code::
BMInOutArray.hardwareInputArray(s, 'Inputs');
::


method:: privateBusBlock
Allocate a new block of private audio busses and return them as a BMInOutArray. This uses the server's normal bus allocator. The link::Classes/Bus:: objects will be stored internally so that their indices can be freed later (see strong::freeBusObjects:: below).

argument:: name
A link::Classes/String:: or link::Classes/Symbol:: to use as the base name.
argument:: size
The number of busses to allocate.
argument:: server
The link::Classes/Server:: whose busses will be allocated.

code::		
p = BMInOutArray.privateBusBlock(\fooBus, 12, s);
p.freeBusObjects; // release my bus indices
::


INSTANCEMETHODS::

method:: keys
Return this array's keys as an link::Classes/Array::.

code::		
a = s.outsAsBMInOutArray;
a.keys;
::

method:: values
Return this array's values as an link::Classes/Array::.
		
code::
a = s.outsAsBMInOutArray;
a.values;
::


method:: addPrivateBusBlock
Add a block of private audio busses to this array. Bus objects will be stored internally so that their indices can be freed later (see strong::freeBusObjects:: below).
		
argument:: name
A String or Symbol to use as the base name.
argument:: size
The number of busses to allocate.
argument:: server
The Server whose busses will be allocated.

code::		
a = s.outsAsBMInOutArray.addPrivateBusBlock(\private, 10, s);
a.freeBusObjects; // release my bus indices
::


method:: freeBusObjects
Free the indices for any Bus objects created using strong::addPrivateBusBlock:: or strong::*privateBusBlock::. You should only do this if you don't plan to use this array and/or its elements again.


method:: add
Add an link::Classes/Association:: or a link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMSpeaker:: to the end of this array.

argument:: assoc
The Association or BMSpeaker to add.

code::		
i = BMInOutArray.new;
i.add(\foo->1); // add an Association
i.add(BMSpeaker(\bar, 2)); // add a BMSpeaker
::


method:: addFirst
Insert an link::Classes/Association:: or a link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMSpeaker:: at the start of this array.

argument:: assoc
The Association or BMSpeaker to insert.
		
code::
i = BMInOutArray.new;
i.add(\foo->1); // add an Association
i.addFirst(BMSpeaker(\bar, 2)); // add a BMSpeaker before \foo
::


method:: insert
Insert an link::Classes/Association:: or a link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMSpeaker::.

argument:: index
The index at which to insert assoc.
argument:: assoc
The Association or BMSpeaker to insert.
		
code::
i = BMInOutArray.new;
i.add(\foo->1); // add an Association
i.add(BMSpeaker(\bar, 2)); // add a BMSpeaker
i.insert(1, BMSpeaker(\foobar, 3)); // insert a BMSpeaker inbetween
::


method:: removeAt
Remove and return the value (i.e. bus index or link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMSpeaker::) specified by key.

argument:: key
The key of the object to be removed.

code::		
i = BMInOutArray.new;
i.add(\foo->1); // add an Association
i.add(BMSpeaker(\bar, 2)); // add a BMSpeaker
i.removeAt(\bar); // remove \bar
::


method:: at	
Return the value (i.e. bus index or link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMSpeaker::) specified by a key or index.

argument:: keyOrIndex
The key or index of the element to be accessed
		
code::
i = BMInOutArray.new;
i.add(\foo->1); // add an Association
i.add(BMSpeaker(\bar, 2)); // add a BMSpeaker
i.at(\foo); // key
i.at(1); // index
i[\foo]; // C-style syntax also works
::

	
method:: put	
Add the value (a bus index or link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMSpeaker::) as an Association with key. In terms of order the Association will be added at the end of the array.

argument:: key
A Symbol to use as the key of the Association. If value is a BMSpeaker its name variable will be set to this.
argument:: value
The bus index or BMSpeaker to be added.
		
code::
i = BMInOutArray.new;
i.put(\foo, 1);
i.put(\bar, BMSpeaker(\bar, 2));
i[\foobar] = 3; // C-style syntax also works
::


method:: putAll
Add all the elements of one or more dictionaries (usually also BMInOutArrays) to this array.

argument:: dictionaries
One or more dictionaries to be added.

code::		
i = BMInOutArray.new;
j = BMInOutArray.privateBusBlock(\foo, 3, s);
i.putAll(j, s.outsAsBMInOutArray);
		
j.freeBusObjects; // release my bus indices
::


method:: keysValuesDo
Iterate over the elements of this array evaluating function.

argument:: function
The Function to be evaluated. This will be passed the key, value, and index of each element as arguments.
		
code::
i = BMInOutArray.privateBusBlock(\foo, 3, s);
i.keysValuesDo({|k, v, i| [k, v, i].postln });
	
i.freeBusObjects; // release my bus indices
::


method:: keysDo 
Iterate over the elements of this array evaluating function.

argument:: function
The Function to be evaluated. This will be passed the key and index of each element as arguments.

code::		
i = BMInOutArray.privateBusBlock(\foo, 3, s);
i.keysDo({|k, i| [k, i].postln });
		
i.freeBusObjects; // release my bus indices
::
		
	
method:: associationsDo
Iterate over the elements of this array evaluating function.

argument:: function
The Function to be evaluated. This will be passed each element (an Association or a BMSpeaker) and the index as arguments.
		
code::
i = BMInOutArray.privateBusBlock(\foo, 3, s);
i.put(\bar, BMSpeaker(\bar, 2));
i.associationsDo({|a, i| [a, i].postln });
		
i.freeBusObjects; // release my bus indices
::


method:: do	
Iterate over the elements of this array evaluating function.

argument:: function
The Function to be evaluated. This will be passed the value and index of each element as arguments.
		
code::
i = BMInOutArray.privateBusBlock(\foo, 3, s);
i.put(\bar, BMSpeaker(\bar, 2));
i.do({|v, i| [v, i].postln });
		
i.freeBusObjects; // release my bus indices
::


method:: collect	
Iterate over the elements of this array evaluating function, and using the results to create a new BMInOutArray.

argument:: function
The Function to be evaluated. This will be passed the value, key, and index of each element as arguments. It should return the new value.
		
code::
i = BMInOutArray.new;
i.put(\foo, BMSpeaker(\foo, 0));
i.put(\bar, BMSpeaker(\bar, 1));
i[\foo].directivity;
i = i.collect({|v, k, i| v.directivity = 'reflected' });
i[\foo].directivity;
::


method:: select
Iterate over the elements of this array evaluating function, adding those items for which function returns true to a new BMInOutArray.

argument:: function
The Function to be evaluated. This will be passed the value, key, and index of each element as arguments. It should return a Boolean indicating whether value should be added to the new BMInOutArray.

code::
i = BMInOutArray.new;
i.put(\foo, BMSpeaker(\foo, 0).directivity = 'reflected');
i.put(\bar, BMSpeaker(\bar, 1).directivity = 'direct');
i = i.select({|v, k, i| v.directivity == 'direct' });
::


method:: reject	
Iterate over the elements of this array evaluating function, adding those items for which function returns false to a new BMInOutArray.

argument:: function
The Function to be evaluated. This will be passed the value, key, and index of each element as arguments. It should return a Boolean indicating whether value should not be added to the new BMInOutArray.
		
code::
i = BMInOutArray.new;
i.put(\foo, BMSpeaker(\foo, 0).directivity = 'reflected');
i.put(\bar, BMSpeaker(\bar, 1).directivity = 'direct');
i = i.reject({|v, k, i| v.directivity == 'direct' });
::


method:: associationsCollectAs
Iterate over the elements of this array evaluating function, and using the results to create a new instances of class.

argument:: function
The Function to be evaluated. This will be passed each element (an Association or a BMSpeaker) and the index as arguments.
argument:: class
The class of the new Collection.
		
code::
i = BMInOutArray.new;
i.put(\foo, BMSpeaker(\foo, 0));
i.put(\bar, BMSpeaker(\bar, 1));
i.put(\foobar, 2);
j = i.associationsCollectAs({|assoc, i| assoc.key ++ " has a bus index of " ++ assoc.value.asUGenInput }, Array);
::


method:: species
Returns the receiver's class, i.e. BMInOutArray.


method:: ++	
Concatenate the receiver with another BMInOutArray, returning a new BMInOutArray

argument:: aBMInOutArray
Explanation of aBMInOutArray. Default value is nil. Other information.
		
code::
i =  s.outsAsBMInOutArray;
j = BMInOutArray.privateBusBlock(\foo, 3, s);
k = i ++ j;
		
j.freeBusObjects; // release my bus indices
::


method:: defineSubArray
Define a subarray which can be accessed by name.

argument:: name
A Symbol indicating the name of the subarray.
argument:: elementNames
An Array of Symbols corresponding to the keys of the elements to be included in this subarray. 

code::		
i = Bus.audio(s, 12).asBMInOutArray(\myPrivateBusaho);
i.defineSubArray(\firstTwo, ['myPrivateBusaho-1', 'myPrivateBusaho-2']);
i.getSubArray(\firstTwo);
::

	

method:: defineSubArrayFromMatch
Define a subarray which can be accessed by name by selecting all elements whose names contain matchText.

argument:: name
A Symbol indicating the name of the subarray.
argument:: matchText
A String or Symbol to match

code::
i = Bus.audio(s, 12).asBMInOutArray(\myPrivateBusaho);
i.addFirst(BMSpeaker(\bar, 2)); // add a BMSpeaker before \foo
i.defineSubArrayFromMatch(\private, "Private");
i.defineSubArrayFromMatch(\bar, "bar");
i.getSubArray(\private);
i.getSubArray(\bar);
::


method:: getSubArray
Returns a new BMInOutArray corresponding to the subarray specified by name.

argument:: name
A Symbol indicating the subarray to retrieve.
	
code::	
i = Bus.audio(s, 12).asBMInOutArray(\myPrivateBusaho);
i.defineSubArray(\firstTwo, ['myPrivateBusaho-1', 'myPrivateBusaho-2']);
i.getSubArray(\firstTwo);
::


method:: getSubArrayKeys
Returns an Array containing the keys of the elements contained in the subarray specified by name.

argument:: name
A Symbol indicating the subarray whose keys will be retrieved.
		
code::
i = Bus.audio(s, 12).asBMInOutArray(\myPrivateBusaho);
i.defineSubArray(\firstTwo, ['myPrivateBusaho-1', 'myPrivateBusaho-2']);
i.getSubArrayKeys(\firstTwo);
::


method:: removeSubArray
Remove an existing subarray from the list of subarrays. (The elements themselves remain in the array).

argument:: name
A Symbol indicating the subarray to remove.
		
code::
i = Bus.audio(s, 12).asBMInOutArray(\myPrivateBusaho);
i.defineSubArray(\firstTwo, ['myPrivateBusaho-1', 'myPrivateBusaho-2']);
i.subArrays;
i.removeSubArray(\firstTwo);
i.subArrays;
::


method:: addToSubArray
Add an element to an existing subarray.

argument:: name
A Symbol indicating the subarray to which the element will be added.
argument:: element
A Symbol corresponding to the key of the element to be added.
		
code::
i = Bus.audio(s, 12).asBMInOutArray(\myPrivateBusaho);
i.defineSubArray(\firstTwo, ['myPrivateBusaho-1', 'myPrivateBusaho-2']);
i.addToSubArray(\firstTwo, 'myPrivateBusaho-3');
i.getSubArrayKeys(\firstTwo);
::


method:: removeFromSubArray
Remove an element from an existing subarray.

argument:: name
A Symbol indicating the subarray from which the element will be removed.
argument:: element
A Symbol corresponding to the key of the element to be removed.

code::		
i = Bus.audio(s, 12).asBMInOutArray(\myPrivateBusaho);
i.defineSubArray(\firstTwo, ['myPrivateBusaho-1', 'myPrivateBusaho-2']);
i.removeFromSubArray(\firstTwo, 'myPrivateBusaho-1');
i.getSubArrayKeys(\firstTwo);
::


method:: subArrays
Returns an Array of Symbols corresponding to the names of all defined subarrays.

code::		
i = Bus.audio(s, 12).asBMInOutArray(\myPrivateBusaho);
i.defineSubArray(\firstTwo, ['myPrivateBusaho-1', 'myPrivateBusaho-2']);
i.defineSubArray(\threeAndFour, ['myPrivateBusaho-3', 'myPrivateBusaho-4']);
i.subArrays;
::


method:: boundaries
Iterate over the array and calculate the smallest rectangular cuboid (aligned with the axes) which can contain all the BMSpeakers in the list. Associations are ignored. Returns an Array of two Arrays in the form [[minX, minY, minZ], [maxX, maxY, maxZ]]
		
		
method:: isBMInOutArray
Returns true. This method is defined in an extension to Object to return false and can thus be used for testing.


method:: asBMInOutArray
Returns the receiver.


method:: asUGenInput
Returns an Array consisting of the bus indices of the receiver's elements. 


method:: asControlInput
Returns an Array consisting of the bus indices of the receiver's elements. 
		
		
method:: asOSCArgArray
Returns an Array consisting of the bus indices of the receiver's elements. 
		
		
method:: asOSCArgBundle
Returns an Array consisting of the bus indices of the receiver's elements. 


